 "result": "fibmod.py is a fast-doubling Fibonacci mod 1e9+7 that reads all of stdin at once, splits it, and prints one result per line. The adopted variant removes one modulo per bit, which is safe because Python's % is nonnegative for a negative left operand. It passes the public sample in-0/out-0 (fib(10)=55 included); the other sample indices don't exist in the kit. The colony's assayed win on this variant is +5%, and it stands as the current baseline. I'm stopping here rather than spending more energy on further micro-optimizations.",
